Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:55:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Document the header frame, the bounded reopen and the
 data barrier

The WAL format documents the header frame (marker HDR1 at trailer offset
52) and what recovery restores from it; the storage-that-cannot-sync
paragraph follows the durability policy. Implementation notes 9 to 11 say
what the header frame restores, which reopens are bounded (decision 13)
and when the data barrier runs (decision 14).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
